cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "opcem — Catalytic Event Microscopy: transport-corrected, beam-aware causal inference from operando electron microscopy of single-atom platinum catalysts"
message: "If you use this software or its protocol, please cite it. Note that all numerical results it produces are simulated."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Angeline"
    given-names: "M. Nisha"
    affiliation: "Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Velalar College of Engineering and Technology, Thindal, Erode, India"
    email: "nishavlsidesign@gmail.com"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - operando electron microscopy
  - single-atom catalysis
  - platinum
  - causal inference
  - mass spectrometry
  - closed-loop control
  - digital twin
abstract: >
  A methodology and in-silico validation for event-resolved structure-activity
  inference in operando electron microscopy of single-atom Pt catalysts.
  Provides a two-level digital twin (kinetic Monte Carlo of one illuminated
  field of view plus a mass-conserving population balance for the whole
  reactive zone), virtual ADF-STEM/EELS/quadrupole-MS instruments, and
  ground-truth validation of eight estimators covering transport
  deconvolution, event-aligned effects, beam-perturbation accounting,
  projection-aware mobility, and closed-loop actuation. All numerical outputs
  are simulated; no physical instrument was operated.
